<title>FRANCE: Usinor Sees 700 Mln Ffr Cash From Vallourec Sale.</title>
<headline>Usinor Sees 700 Mln Ffr Cash From Vallourec Sale.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Usinor Sacilor Finance Director Robert Houdry said on Tuesday sale of the steelmaker's entire stake in steel tube maker Vallourec would generate around 700 million francs in cash during 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The sale of our position in Vallourec which will be enacted in 1997 as soon as the European Commission authorisation comes, and assuming we will sell the remaining...will bring 700 million francs more or less in cash during 1997,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>He was speaking in an interview with Reuters Financial Television.</p>
</text>
